{"title":"2025 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2025 AMC 10B #1</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">2025 AMC 12B #1</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_-_Cheese_(Sort_of)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 - Cheese (Sort of)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:20)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:20)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The instructions on a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ceffeb3d880c80aa8bb29fe99a7905ca0b2f719.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$350$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />-gram bag of coffee beans say that proper brewing of a large mug of pour-over coffee requires <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> grams of coffee beans. What is the greatest number of properly brewed large mugs of coffee that can be made from the coffee beans in that bag?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/3/a93cc67156f3631e62d79ba1e353cc3d62047547.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 16 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 17 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 18 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 19 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cd3947c8cb2961b12eabbda118f4d1796e3be4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{350}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/2/93235f4c01f02ecb7fd7c8ce6ddb4be81bb3ed70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />. We round down to find the maximum he can make (he cannot brew half of a cup), so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/041c07f811ae43e46d24cb06a605761f96fc6397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~mingbaboo (this is my first time doing this so it could be very wrong)\n</p><p>~NumberNinja1234 (Minor Latex and grammar edit for clarity)&#160;:)\n</p><p>~Sumeete (Minor grammar edits)\n</p><p>~SharkBlueHorse (Minor grammar edits)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eea83521b9e585be335f2a1db9eafb6e4cfe19b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$340$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />-grams if we use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> mugs. This is because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/39676eec6d1fcf6590e589cdc0ebbe74fb85aa6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\cdot 17 = 340$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />. We cannot use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because that would mean using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c62a47cbc153efdf4611d8660429ea879be3f192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />-grams. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/041c07f811ae43e46d24cb06a605761f96fc6397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>Note that you can also find this by finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/7/f176d6df2030b6685363a9c6b09c50faa541f74c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\frac{350}{20} \\rfloor = 17.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~lprado\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ceffeb3d880c80aa8bb29fe99a7905ca0b2f719.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$350$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> with a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> grams cannot make a properly brewed large mug of coffee, as stated in the problem. We can only count fully brewed mugs of coffee, hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/041c07f811ae43e46d24cb06a605761f96fc6397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Yoonyoung11\n~Minor edits and Latex by Yvz2900\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_-_Cheese_.28Sort_of.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_-_Cheese_(Sort_of)\">Solution 4 - Cheese (Sort of)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 - Cheese (Sort of)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> by each of the answer choices to see if we can find which one is closest and under <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d5b05ee1b60a6073ae6b79f25637b68879b78ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$350.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> First, we try solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c43070a2acf8f4e25d98e48c404d9348a26d40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0f9e3ddc25b65cef1985727f97935dc848ae19c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\cdot 20 = 320,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> off from 350, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c43070a2acf8f4e25d98e48c404d9348a26d40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> cannot be the answer, because we can add another <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Moving on to answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43d667a133a3abb21d1e286bebd9c49f7fcc0291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{B},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/9/bc99d1b89863230bf92f7dfa3280f7cc2e8df0c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 \\cdot 20 = 340.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" /> We notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/e/29e7d1bc65c760fc26357b3bdec46d29a6c40f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$350-340=10,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" /> and so we cannot add another <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to get closer but less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d5b05ee1b60a6073ae6b79f25637b68879b78ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$350.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> (The next number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, would result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cf3b55deb11dc7979f8c51f0e6e2bbe824fc1e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\cdot 18=360,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" /> which is more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ceffeb3d880c80aa8bb29fe99a7905ca0b2f719.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$350$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.) So, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/041c07f811ae43e46d24cb06a605761f96fc6397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>(note - the actual cheese solution would likely include every single answer choice, but I use a bit of intellect in this solution)\n</p><p>~zoyashaikh\n</p><p>~edited by SmartyDigits\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E0:20.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:20)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:20)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:20)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/gFNczjnj2DY\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/gFNczjnj2DY</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/s-Wimgu9wto\">https://youtu.be/s-Wimgu9wto</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w3WECKtp0FM\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w3WECKtp0FM</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aZS3YClnhFY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aZS3YClnhFY</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><